00:39:12,840 --> 00:39:13,900
Learning a language.

567
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,880
You'll be able to talk
to foreigners then.

568
00:39:18,490 --> 00:39:19,320
Yes.

569
00:39:20,130 --> 00:39:21,480
Right now,

570
00:39:21,740 --> 00:39:24,160
Gear has gotten so much better.

571
00:39:28,510 --> 00:39:31,390
Gramps, your place
has a nice atmosphere.

572
00:39:31,410 --> 00:39:33,400
Is there any table left for me?

573
00:39:34,150 --> 00:39:36,000
Come, follow me.
I'll take you to your table.

574
00:39:56,000 --> 00:39:58,560
Hello, everyone. Today,

575
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:00,920
I'm not here alone, because I have

576
00:40:01,130 --> 00:40:04,650
a newbie yet passionate dancer
who will compete in PK with me.

577
00:40:08,220 --> 00:40:09,430
[Hi]

578
00:40:09,450 --> 00:40:10,490
[Hello, Jay]

579
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:12,140
[Hello]

580
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,440
I think everyone wants to know

581
00:40:24,790 --> 00:40:27,870
who our passionate newbie dancer is,

582
00:40:28,120 --> 00:40:29,120
right?

583
00:40:29,210 --> 00:40:32,480
Then, please welcome
our dancer. Come on.

584
00:40:34,660 --> 00:40:35,960
Come on.

585
00:40:36,270 --> 00:40:37,030
No.

586
00:40:39,890 --> 00:40:43,470
Um, I'll be back in a minute.

587
00:40:43,490 --> 00:40:44,930
Please don't go anywhere.

588
00:40:44,950 --> 00:40:46,470
I won't take long.

589
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:48,200
Pond,

590
00:40:48,950 --> 00:40:51,400
what the hell are you doing?
Didn't we agree to this?

591
00:40:51,570 --> 00:40:53,560
I don't want to do it anymore.

592
00:40:55,110 --> 00:40:56,110
Fine,

593
00:40:56,990 --> 00:40:58,310
but I'll tell your mom

594
00:40:59,140 --> 00:41:01,330
that you asked her for
field trip money

595
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:05,360
but you actually
spent it on game skins.

596
00:41:05,670 --> 00:41:07,200
I'll tell her everything.

597
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:09,720
3, 2...

598
00:41:10,060 --> 00:41:12,180
Alright, fine.

599
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:13,320
Come this way.

600
00:41:13,460 --> 00:41:15,030
Here he is, everyone.

601
00:41:15,050 --> 00:41:17,360
The face of our new dancer.

602
00:41:17,390 --> 00:41:18,480
So? Isn't he cute?

603
00:41:18,500 --> 00:41:19,080
[Ooh, he's cute]

604
00:41:19,100 --> 00:41:20,790
Can you introduce yourself
to the fans?

605
00:41:24,340 --> 00:41:25,440
Hello,

606
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:27,160
I'm Pond.

607
00:41:27,240 --> 00:41:28,760
I didn't want to dance.

608
00:41:29,380 --> 00:41:31,080
- I was forced to be here.
- Oh.

609
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:34,120
Oh, Pond. You're shy, aren't you?

610
00:41:34,250 --> 00:41:36,190
Um, everyone. I'll have to start
by saying that

611
00:41:36,210 --> 00:41:39,240
this is Pond's first time doing this.
So he might be shy...

612
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:40,480
That's why he made those jokes,

613
00:41:40,860 --> 00:41:41,980
- right?
- I'm not joking around.

614
00:41:42,460 --> 00:41:45,600
Um, it's time for the fun.

615
00:41:45,740 --> 00:41:48,130
If you want to see me dance,

616
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:49,680
send in the roses.

617
00:41:49,890 --> 00:41:52,480
But if you want to see Pond dance,

618
00:41:52,710 --> 00:41:54,560
send in the ice creams.

619
00:41:54,950 --> 00:41:57,070
The person with the most gifts

620
00:41:57,420 --> 00:42:00,200
will perform solo
after this freestyle dance.

621
00:42:02,750 --> 00:42:04,170
Please send us a lot of gifts.

622
00:42:04,190 --> 00:42:07,630
Then... let's dance freestyle.

623
00:42:07,890 --> 00:42:08,880
Are you ready, Pond?

624
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:10,680
Ready? Go!

625
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:17,680
Go, dance.

626
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:29,800
Send us gifts, alright?

627
00:42:29,820 --> 00:42:30,280
[Aw]

628
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:31,750
Dance.

629
00:42:31,770 --> 00:42:33,760
Come on, dance.

630
00:42:33,780 --> 00:42:35,640
[How cute]

631
00:42:35,660 --> 00:42:37,140
[LOL]

632
00:42:37,160 --> 00:42:39,350
Move around. Twerk.

633
00:42:54,620 --> 00:42:57,280
Does your granddad
dance for your customers?

634
00:42:59,300 --> 00:43:00,270
That's nice.

635
00:43:02,600 --> 00:43:04,230
But why is his
dance partner a guy?

636
00:43:07,820 --> 00:43:09,110
That isn't a show.

637
00:43:09,790 --> 00:43:11,480
It's an opening dance.

638
00:43:14,770 --> 00:43:17,230
The person dancing with Granddad
is Grandpa Kasaem.

639
00:43:18,080 --> 00:43:19,040
He's Granddad's boyfriend.

640
00:43:21,340 --> 00:43:23,080
They've been dancing like this

641
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:25,040
ever since I can remember.

642
00:43:26,870 --> 00:43:27,830
"Boyfriend"?

643
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:32,830
No,

644
00:43:34,060 --> 00:43:35,060
that's his partner for life.

645
00:43:41,610 --> 00:43:42,880
When are you going home?

646
00:43:46,780 --> 00:43:48,160
Are you pushing me away?

647
00:43:50,480 --> 00:43:52,400
I'm your customer today.

648
00:43:52,770 --> 00:43:53,470
Oh,

649
00:43:54,240 --> 00:43:55,560
in case you forgot,

650
00:43:56,240 --> 00:43:58,680
your granddad asked you
to sit with me.

651
00:43:59,910 --> 00:44:01,950
He'd be sad

652
00:44:02,600 --> 00:44:04,430
if you tell his customer to go home.

653
00:44:13,180 --> 00:44:14,200
Mr. Kanthi,

654
00:44:14,670 --> 00:44:15,870
please leave.

655
00:44:16,280 --> 00:44:17,200
I beg of you.

656
00:44:18,120 --> 00:44:19,000
No,

657
00:44:20,230 --> 00:44:21,790
not until I get an answer

658
00:44:21,980 --> 00:44:24,200
about why my student
is skipping class today.

659
00:44:45,560 --> 00:44:47,190
There are hosts here, too?

660
00:44:49,030 --> 00:44:49,880
Hosts?

661
00:44:51,800 --> 00:44:53,160
Our restaurant doesn't
have any hosts, though?

662
00:44:54,300 --> 00:44:55,160
There.

663
00:45:00,840 --> 00:45:01,590
Oh,

664
00:45:02,230 --> 00:45:03,280
that's Grandpa Aek.

665
00:45:04,210 --> 00:45:05,680
He's a veteran soldier.

666
00:45:06,440 --> 00:45:08,590
He usually brings his boys
to hang out here.

667
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:12,960
I'll be like that when I'm old.

668
00:45:13,500 --> 00:45:15,400
Old, but still spicy.

669
00:45:17,780 --> 00:45:18,760
You are already old.

670
00:45:19,840 --> 00:45:20,560
I can hear you.

671
00:45:38,900 --> 00:45:39,700
Gear.

672
00:45:40,230 --> 00:45:40,920
Yes.

673
00:45:42,740 --> 00:45:45,920
Have you ever thought about
what to do after graduation?

674
00:45:50,880 --> 00:45:52,320
I haven't decided yet.

675
00:45:53,790 --> 00:45:56,680
I'll probably take care of this restaurant.

676
00:45:58,560 --> 00:46:00,440
What about you?

677
00:46:02,080 --> 00:46:03,560
I want to own this restaurant.

678
00:46:05,560 --> 00:46:06,320
Huh?

679
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:10,160
Are you going to buy my
Grandpa's restaurant?

680
00:46:12,290 --> 00:46:14,040
I'm going to be a
son-in-law in your family.

681
00:46:17,300 --> 00:46:18,080
Gear,

682
00:46:19,840 --> 00:46:21,440
after you graduate, let's get married.

683
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:27,800
Kim...

684
00:46:30,160 --> 00:46:31,750
Let's be together until we're old

685
00:46:31,770 --> 00:46:33,200
like your granddad
and grandpa, alright?

686
00:47:07,480 --> 00:47:08,400
Gear,

687
00:47:10,200 --> 00:47:11,380
will you dance with me?

688
00:47:15,760 --> 00:47:16,760
So?

689
00:48:11,370 --> 00:48:12,440
I'm sorry.

690
00:48:15,160 --> 00:48:15,800
For what?

691
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:20,560
For upsetting you.

692
00:48:31,190 --> 00:48:32,480
If you want to cry,

693
00:48:33,320 --> 00:48:34,400
just let it out.

694
00:48:42,620 --> 00:48:49,760
♫I used to think love was just a mirage♫

695
00:48:50,250 --> 00:48:57,840
♫What people have said must
have been a dreamy facade♫

696
00:48:58,730 --> 00:49:02,260
♫Thank you for teaching me♫

697
00:49:02,290 --> 00:49:06,360
♫What love can be♫

698
00:49:06,380 --> 00:49:08,640
♫"Love" used to mean nothing,♫

699
00:49:08,660 --> 00:49:13,900
♫But now it's starting to have a meaning♫

700
00:49:13,920 --> 00:49:17,420
♫The love you gave me♫

701
00:49:17,450 --> 00:49:22,000
♫Was very fulfilling, you helped me realize♫

702
00:49:22,040 --> 00:49:29,400
♫That this love is meant for you and me♫

703
00:49:31,610 --> 00:49:32,660
I'm going to Bang Saen.

704
00:49:32,680 --> 00:49:34,870
Bang Saen? Are you fucking nuts?

705
00:49:35,410 --> 00:49:36,280
Nu,

706
00:49:36,630 --> 00:49:38,960
- I'll see you later.
- See you later, Nu.

707
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:40,200
- Get home safely. See you.
- Huh?

708
00:49:40,430 --> 00:49:41,920
Nu, you're not going home yet?

709
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:43,880
Oh? You're not going?

710
00:49:44,420 --> 00:49:46,880
- Then we'll get going.
- Yeah, bye.

711
00:49:50,640 --> 00:49:52,880
How are you going home today?
Want me to take you home?

712
00:49:54,630 --> 00:49:56,720
Maybe next time.

713
00:49:57,400 --> 00:49:59,200
I'm waiting for my boyfriend.

714
00:50:10,680 --> 00:50:12,280
Oh? Why...

715
00:50:12,740 --> 00:50:14,120
Why didn't you leave with Zee?

716
00:50:14,660 --> 00:50:16,590
I'll keep you company.

717
00:50:17,160 --> 00:50:19,110
I'll leave when your boyfriend arrives.

718
00:50:20,520 --> 00:50:22,440
Oh, is that alright with you?

719
00:50:35,840 --> 00:50:36,600
Boss,

720
00:50:37,040 --> 00:50:38,610
I sent you the information

721
00:50:39,030 --> 00:50:41,320
you asked me to investigate.

722
00:50:45,630 --> 00:50:48,280
Shin just came back from overseas.

723
00:50:49,270 --> 00:50:50,990
Chai has never taken him
to any events,

724
00:50:51,010 --> 00:50:52,120
because he's his illegitimate son.

725
00:50:52,860 --> 00:50:56,080
Ever since his eldest son passed
from an accident,

726
00:50:57,620 --> 00:50:59,690
Chai tried to push Shin

727
00:50:59,710 --> 00:51:01,240
to become his successor.

728
00:51:12,150 --> 00:51:13,080
Thanks a lot.

729
00:51:13,850 --> 00:51:14,780
Yes, Boss.

730
00:51:33,120 --> 00:51:35,000
You've been waiting
for half an hour now.

731
00:51:36,150 --> 00:51:37,840
I don't think he's coming.

732
00:51:44,780 --> 00:51:46,140
He said he's on his way.

733
00:51:46,900 --> 00:51:47,880
He's almost here.

734
00:51:50,680 --> 00:51:51,560
There.

735
00:51:57,240 --> 00:51:58,280
Sorry,

736
00:51:58,770 --> 00:52:00,320
I was too invested in the
livestream.

737
00:52:00,660 --> 00:52:01,840
- My bad.
- Mm.

738
00:52:02,080 --> 00:52:02,960
It's okay.

739
00:52:04,040 --> 00:52:04,640
Let's go.

740
00:52:05,600 --> 00:52:07,920
Try to get here on time, will you?

741
00:52:08,350 --> 00:52:10,350
You shouldn't let my friend
sit here waiting for you.

742
00:52:14,240 --> 00:52:15,080
Bank.

743
00:52:19,920 --> 00:52:21,400
Thanks for the advice.

744
00:52:22,420 --> 00:52:23,960
But even Nu hasn't said anything.

745
00:52:26,440 --> 00:52:27,680
So how is this your business?

746
00:52:28,410 --> 00:52:30,680
I just don't want my friend to
sit here and wait for someone.

747
00:52:31,380 --> 00:52:33,000
If you can't drive him around,

748
00:52:33,220 --> 00:52:34,180
then don't.

749
00:52:34,570 --> 00:52:35,520
I can do it.

750
00:52:48,270 --> 00:52:50,960
Your granddad and grandpa's
restaurant is pretty heartwarming.

751
00:52:52,040 --> 00:52:53,120
I never thought

752
00:52:53,650 --> 00:52:55,120
there'd be a place like this.

753
00:52:55,940 --> 00:52:57,160
I'll visit here again.

754
00:53:00,920 --> 00:53:01,720
Oh,

755
00:53:02,640 --> 00:53:04,240
where should we meet tomorrow?

756
00:53:05,040 --> 00:53:06,080
Should it be Rose Club?

757
00:53:06,480 --> 00:53:07,880
Or my condo?

758
00:53:13,520 --> 00:53:14,680
Um...

759
00:53:15,570 --> 00:53:16,760
I...

760
00:53:17,640 --> 00:53:19,520
Are you still mad about yesterday?

761
00:53:22,280 --> 00:53:24,280
I don't know what I did wrong.

762
00:53:25,240 --> 00:53:27,080
But if you think I was too harsh,

763
00:53:28,460 --> 00:53:29,930
feel free to insult me

764
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:32,360
to make yourself feel better.

765
00:53:32,500 --> 00:53:33,560
So we can be even.

766
00:53:38,480 --> 00:53:39,320
Fine.

767
00:53:41,120 --> 00:53:42,550
You're crazy, heartless,

768
00:53:42,570 --> 00:53:44,760
cocky, pretentious, narcissistic, irritating!

769
00:53:45,010 --> 00:53:46,840
Your words are harsh as
if you're angry all the time.

770
00:53:47,040 --> 00:53:49,540
Do you think the world
revolves around you or something?

771
00:53:49,570 --> 00:53:51,920
You always keep a cold face,

772
00:53:51,950 --> 00:53:55,600
but actually, you're just a pretentious
guy acting all tough.

773
00:53:56,180 --> 00:53:57,600
You're a broken microwave!

774
00:53:57,620 --> 00:53:58,900
You can't heat things up properly,

775
00:53:58,920 --> 00:54:00,200
and you even black out.

776
00:54:00,420 --> 00:54:02,700
Stop acting like you're the most
handsome guy already.

777
00:54:02,720 --> 00:54:03,800
It's annoying!

778
00:54:08,420 --> 00:54:09,440
Why are you quiet?

779
00:54:10,060 --> 00:54:11,000
Go on.

780
00:54:13,730 --> 00:54:15,360
I'm not mad at you,

781
00:54:18,540 --> 00:54:19,810
because what you said

782
00:54:20,220 --> 00:54:21,320
was not wrong.

783
00:54:23,780 --> 00:54:25,200
I have to thank you

784
00:54:25,440 --> 00:54:26,720
for reminding me.

785
00:54:33,800 --> 00:54:35,320
Then tomorrow...

786
00:54:35,460 --> 00:54:37,200
I don't want to learn about
sex from you anymore.

787
00:54:44,030 --> 00:54:44,840
Gear?

788
00:54:46,090 --> 00:54:48,360
I'm sorry for wasting your time.

789
00:54:49,110 --> 00:54:49,960
And...

790
00:54:50,560 --> 00:54:51,920
thank you for everything.

791
00:55:08,290 --> 00:55:16,200
♫That this love is meant for you and me♫

792
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:19,480
Here, this is for you.

793
00:55:19,620 --> 00:55:20,800
Mr. Kanthi?

794
00:55:21,440 --> 00:55:22,040
What?

795
00:55:22,060 --> 00:55:23,760
You asked him to teach you about sex,

796
00:55:23,800 --> 00:55:25,740
but you don't want to learn
that from him anymore.

797
00:55:25,760 --> 00:55:27,120
Is that why he's following you around?

798
00:55:27,400 --> 00:55:28,880
When will you stop running away?

799
00:55:28,900 --> 00:55:31,040
Why are you following me, then?

800
00:55:32,400 --> 00:55:33,600
Are you ready, my love?

801
00:55:33,760 --> 00:55:34,840
I've been ready since yesterday.

802
00:55:35,360 --> 00:55:36,920
Hold on tight, alright?

803
00:55:37,160 --> 00:55:38,280
I'm going to take you for a spin.

804
00:55:39,040 --> 00:55:40,200
Mr. Shin,

805
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:42,680
where should we go after dinner?

806
00:55:42,920 --> 00:55:44,160
You can decide for us, Ms. Mei.

807
00:55:44,640 --> 00:55:46,320
Let's go see a movie, then.

808
00:56:02,380 --> 00:56:05,760
♫Thank you for teaching me♫

809
00:56:05,780 --> 00:56:09,860
♫What love can be♫

810
00:56:09,880 --> 00:56:12,120
♫"Love" used to mean nothing,♫

811
00:56:12,140 --> 00:56:17,460
♫But now it's starting to have a meaning♫

812
00:56:17,480 --> 00:56:20,980
♫The love you gave me♫

813
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:25,380
♫Was very fulfilling, you helped me realize♫

814
00:56:25,400 --> 00:56:33,020
♫That this love is meant for you and me♫
